WEBVTT

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.130
Christ will return for two main purposes.

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:10.210
First, to take the believers who are
mature in life as His bride.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:20.470
Second, to deal with all injustice and
establish His thousand-year kingdom on
earth.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:28.230
Revelation 20:6 says that those who share
in the first resurrection are blessed.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:35.355
Why the first resurrection? This is the
outstanding resurrection spoken of in

00:00:35.355 --> 00:00:36.210
Philippians.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.970
Think of attending a graduation ceremony.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:46.230
Those who have done especially well
receive special honors.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:52.570
These people are blessed. They will reign
with Christ for a thousand years.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:03.498
Those who are mature and ready will enter
the thousand-year kingdom and reign with

00:01:03.498 --> 00:01:04.590
the Lord.

00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:11.770
Those who are not yet mature will go
through a period of further learning.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:20.312
The millennial kingdom rewards the
overcoming believers and gives the
immature an

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.070
opportunity to grow.

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:29.070
After the millennium, all believers will
be mature and enter the eternity of the
new

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.490
heaven and new earth.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:39.783
Revelation 21:2 describes the holy city,
New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:40.740
from God.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.160
She is prepared as a bride adorned for her
husband.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.660
The holy city, New Jerusalem, here is not
heaven.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:02:00.040
Many Christians have not studied the Bible
carefully and assume this means heaven.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:06.913
That is not what it means. Over the past
two thousand years, in every saved and

00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:08.740
regenerated believer,

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:13.100
God desires to make His home in our
hearts. We become His dwelling place.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:20.871
God also becomes our dwelling place. We
abide in Christ and receive His rich
supply

00:02:20.871 --> 00:02:21.620
of life.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:29.320
The New Jerusalem is a sign of the mutual
dwelling place of God and humanity.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.780
It also signifies a bride adorned for her
husband.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:43.480
To match her husband, the bride must share
his life and nature.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:50.720
She must also grow in life, because the
Lord Jesus is coming as the Bridegroom.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:59.040
He cannot marry a two-year-old girl. She
must grow and become mature.
